The RdRp Summit brings together researchers working on diverse RNA virus systems, from virus discovery and taxonomy to molecular mechanisms, structural insights, and computational approaches.

## Save the date

The 2027 summit runs on **Friday 12 and Saturday 13 March 2027** in Jena, Germany, directly after [ViBioM 2027](https://evbc.uni-jena.de/event/international-virus-bioinformatics-meeting-2027-vibiom/) (9-11 March), which marks the tenth anniversary of the European Virus Bioinformatics Center. Attending both meetings on a single trip is the intended design.

The meeting is planned as a hybrid event, with on-site capacity for up to 150 participants and a broadcast for remote attendees.

## Building on two previous summits

The first summit (Valencia, 2023) drew over 70 participants from more than 50 research institutions, half of them early career researchers. The second (Lisbon, 2025) was supported by ISME, which funded travel grants for early career researchers. Each summit has produced a community consensus statement.

Between summits, the community runs a monthly [RNA Virus Discovery Journal Club](/journal-club/) and several open study groups covering benchmarking, phylogeny, and host-virus interactions.

## What is still being decided

Programme, invited speakers, registration and abstract deadlines, and fees are being worked out by the organising committee. This page will be updated as each is settled.
